; DeepSeek-V4 heterogeneous stack recipes from the actual tensor table.
; Each layer reads its expert count and separate gate/up/down formats, token-table
; or biased-top-k routing, and ordinary or compressed RoPE configuration.
; Routing weights use unbiased probabilities; pruning is carried by the bias.
; Four hyper-connection streams pass through both frames at every layer, with
; a separate ordered KV history for each layer and each supplied token.
;
; Independent Form fp64 decoding and control: form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-oracle-stack.bml.
; GPU arithmetic is authored separately; actual and injected executions retain
; their own intermediate outputs and history. Every dispatch is sentinelled and
; checked against its unchanged numerical bound and input-perturbation envelope.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-kv-cache.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-compressor.fk form-stdlib/ds4-order-match.fk native/metal/dsv4-layer-real.fk
;
; Proven by: native/metal/metal_dsv4_stack_oracle.sh.

(do
    ; The real-stack decode seam: the cache append is authored by the Form body and compiled as its
    ; own translation unit. The carrier only binds a layer's arena and the current absolute position.
    ; Keeping it separate avoids adding host-authored Metal to the 43-layer runner.
    ; The COMPRESSED cache rides in the same unit: it is the second lane of the same seam, and the
    ; carrier binds both from the same place. dsv4-compressor.fk holds the recipe and the text.
    (defn dsv4-stack-kv-source ()
            (str_concat "#include <metal_stdlib>\n"
                    (str_concat (dkv-append-msl-body)
                    (str_concat "kernel void form_dsv4_control_logit_adapter (device float* logits [[buffer(0)]], device const float* weights [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& first [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& count [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i < count) logits[first + i] += weights[i]; } "
                                (str_concat (dcp-msl-appendix) (dom-msl-appendix))))))
    (defn dsv4-stack-kv-unit ()
        (do
            (print "MSL")
            (print (dsv4-stack-kv-source))
            (print "END")
            0))

    ; --- the one new kernel the stack needs: BIASED TOP-K selection with UNBIASED weighting.
    ; ds4.c:10665 layer_topk_selected_experts_from_probs, transcribed including topk_desc's (:10630)
    ; exact insertion order and its tie rule (strict >, so the EARLIER index keeps its place).
    ;
    ; THE ASYMMETRY IS LOAD-BEARING and it is why this cannot be the hash kernel with a sort bolted on:
    ; the bias enters the SELECTION score and never the WEIGHT. weight[j] = probs[selected[j]] is the
    ; UNBIASED prob. A kernel that weighted by the biased score would be right-shaped, right-magnitude
    ; and silently wrong — the independent Form reference observes this distinction.
    ;
    ; probs[] uses the SAME stable softplus as form_dsv4_hash_weights (ds4.c:10424): z above 20 passes
    ; through, z below -20 is exp(z), otherwise ln(1+exp(z)). dm_exp / dm_ln / dm_sqrt are the enclosing
    ; unit's spine, so there is exactly ONE softplus and ONE sqrt on the device.
    ;
    ; The fixed arrays cap ne<=256 and nused<=8; above that the kernel WRITES NOTHING, so an overrun is
    ; a refusal the sentinel catches, never a silent stomp (aporon).
    ; SPLIT: the 256 softplus+sqrt evaluations are elementwise-independent and were running on ONE
    ; thread with a 2 KB private array; the selection that follows is a cheap compare loop. ds4 does the
    ; same job in one 256-thread threadgroup with no sort at all (metal/dsv4_misc.metal:4828) and its
    ; router stage costs ~1.8 ms a token against our 48 ms — a 27x gap on identical work. Splitting
    ; keeps the selection order and its strict-> first-index-wins tie rule exactly, so the choice is
    ; bit-identical; only the arithmetic pass parallelises.
    ; AND THE SELECTION WAS STILL THE EXPENSIVE HALF, which the split did not say and ablation did:
    ; skipping form_dsv4_topk_select and form_dsv4_hash_weights takes the token's GPU floor from 40 ms
    ; to 37, over FORTY-THREE dispatches. That is 70 us apiece to compare 256 floats — about two
    ; thousand instructions of arithmetic. It is not the compare loop. It is `sc[i]` read from device
    ; memory 256 times, one at a time, by one thread, each read waited on before the next begins,
    ; because the `continue` makes the loop's next step depend on the value just fetched. Nothing else
    ; in the stack can cover that latency: it is one thread, so there is no other warp to run.
    ;
    ; The fix is not to parallelise the selection — the strict-> first-index-wins rule is what makes
    ; the choice reproducible and a tree would have to re-derive it. It is to stop paying device
    ; latency for the reads. 256 threads fetch sc[] and probs[] into threadgroup memory, which is on
    ; the core; they meet at a barrier; then thread 0 runs THE SAME SCAN, in the same order, over the
    ; same values, out of a memory that answers in a few cycles instead of a few hundred nanoseconds.
    ; The comparisons, the tie rule, the shift-down, the sum and the normalisation are character for
    ; character the ones above, so the six experts chosen and their weights are bit-identical.
    ; AND THE SCAN WAS STILL PAYING DEVICE LATENCY, on the other side. Staging sc[] and probs[] moved
    ; the INPUT onto the core; the six slots the scan carries — idx[8] and val[8], indexed by a loop
    ; whose bound is the runtime `nused` and shifted by an inner loop whose bound is the runtime `j` —
    ; never left it. A thread array the compiler cannot resolve to constants does not live in
    ; registers; it lives in the thread's own device-backed stack, and every `val[j]` in that scan is a
    ; device round trip. FORM_DS4_DOUBLE priced the kernel at 1.6 ms of a 39 ms token over 43 asks —
    ; 37 us to walk 256 floats, the same order as the attention scores over a million multiply-adds.
    ;
    ; The remedy is the one hc-split-seq4-body already used on the Sinkhorn: make the width LITERAL so
    ; the compiler unrolls, every index becomes a constant, and the slots live in registers. Here they
    ; are not even an array — six named ints and six named floats, and the shift-down written out. The
    ; comparisons, the first-index-wins tie rule, the shift, the ascending sum, the 2^-14 floor and the
    ; normalisation are character for character the general kernel's; only nused's six is now a number
    ; the compiler can see. The general kernel stays, serves any other nused, and is the A/B.
    (defn dsv4-topk-select-tg6-body ()
        "kernel void form_dsv4_topk_select_tg6 (device const float* probs [[buffer(0)]], device const float* sc [[buffer(1)]], device uint* ids [[buffer(2)]], device float* wts [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& ne [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& nused [[buffer(5)]], constant float& wscale [[buffer(6)]], uint tid [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint tsz [[threads_per_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float ts[256]; threadgroup float tp[256]; if (ne <= 256u) { for (uint i = tid; i < ne; i += tsz) { ts[i] = sc[i]; tp[i] = probs[i]; } } threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (tid != 0u) return; if (ne > 256u) return; if (nused != 6u) return; if (nused > ne) return; int i0 = -1; int i1 = -1; int i2 = -1; int i3 = -1; int i4 = -1; int i5 = -1; float v0 = 0.0f; float v1 = 0.0f; float v2 = 0.0f; float v3 = 0.0f; float v4 = 0.0f; float v5 = 0.0f; for (uint i = 0u; i < ne; ++i) { float si = ts[i]; if (i5 >= 0 && !(si > v5)) continue; if (i0 < 0 || si > v0) { i5 = i4; v5 = v4; i4 = i3; v4 = v3; i3 = i2; v3 = v2; i2 = i1; v2 = v1; i1 = i0; v1 = v0; i0 = int(i); v0 = si; } else if (i1 < 0 || si > v1) { i5 = i4; v5 = v4; i4 = i3; v4 = v3; i3 = i2; v3 = v2; i2 = i1; v2 = v1; i1 = int(i); v1 = si; } else if (i2 < 0 || si > v2) { i5 = i4; v5 = v4; i4 = i3; v4 = v3; i3 = i2; v3 = v2; i2 = int(i); v2 = si; } else if (i3 < 0 || si > v3) { i5 = i4; v5 = v4; i4 = i3; v4 = v3; i3 = int(i); v3 = si; } else if (i4 < 0 || si > v4) { i5 = i4; v5 = v4; i4 = int(i); v4 = si; } else if (i5 < 0 || si > v5) { i5 = int(i); v5 = si; } } float s0 = 0.0f; s0 = s0 + tp[i0]; s0 = s0 + tp[i1]; s0 = s0 + tp[i2]; s0 = s0 + tp[i3]; s0 = s0 + tp[i4]; s0 = s0 + tp[i5]; float s = (s0 < 0.00006103515625f) ? 0.00006103515625f : s0; ids[0] = uint(i0); wts[0] = tp[i0] / s * wscale; ids[1] = uint(i1); wts[1] = tp[i1] / s * wscale; ids[2] = uint(i2); wts[2] = tp[i2] / s * wscale; ids[3] = uint(i3); wts[3] = tp[i3] / s * wscale; ids[4] = uint(i4); wts[4] = tp[i4] / s * wscale; ids[5] = uint(i5); wts[5] = tp[i5] / s * wscale; } ")

    (defn dsv4-topk-select-tg-body ()
        "kernel void form_dsv4_topk_select_tg (device const float* probs [[buffer(0)]], device const float* sc [[buffer(1)]], device uint* ids [[buffer(2)]], device float* wts [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& ne [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& nused [[buffer(5)]], constant float& wscale [[buffer(6)]], uint tid [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint tsz [[threads_per_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float ts[256]; threadgroup float tp[256]; if (ne <= 256u) { for (uint i = tid; i < ne; i += tsz) { ts[i] = sc[i]; tp[i] = probs[i]; } } threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (tid != 0u) return; if (ne > 256u) return; if (nused > 8u) return; if (nused > ne) return; int idx[8]; float val[8]; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { idx[j] = -1; val[j] = 0.0f; } uint last = nused - 1u; for (uint i = 0u; i < ne; ++i) { float si = ts[i]; if (idx[last] >= 0 && !(si > val[last])) continue; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { if (idx[j] < 0 || si > val[j]) { for (uint mm = nused - 1u; mm > j; --mm) { idx[mm] = idx[mm - 1u]; val[mm] = val[mm - 1u]; } idx[j] = int(i); val[j] = si; break; } } } float s0 = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { s0 = s0 + tp[idx[j]]; } float s = (s0 < 0.00006103515625f) ? 0.00006103515625f : s0; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { ids[j] = uint(idx[j]); wts[j] = tp[idx[j]] / s * wscale; } } ")

    (defn dsv4-topk-split-body ()
        "kernel void form_dsv4_topk_probs (device const float* logits [[buffer(0)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(1)]], device float* probs [[buffer(2)]], device float* sc [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& ne [[buffer(4)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= ne) return; float z = logits[i]; float sp = (z > 20.0f) ? z : ((z < -20.0f) ? dm_exp(z) : dm_ln(1.0f + dm_exp(z))); float p = dm_sqrt(sp); probs[i] = p; sc[i] = p + bias[i]; } kernel void form_dsv4_topk_select (device const float* probs [[buffer(0)]], device const float* sc [[buffer(1)]], device uint* ids [[buffer(2)]], device float* wts [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& ne [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& nused [[buffer(5)]], constant float& wscale [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (gid != 0u) return; if (nused > 8u) return; if (nused > ne) return; int idx[8]; float val[8]; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { idx[j] = -1; val[j] = 0.0f; } uint last = nused - 1u; for (uint i = 0u; i < ne; ++i) { float si = sc[i]; if (idx[last] >= 0 && !(si > val[last])) continue; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { if (idx[j] < 0 || si > val[j]) { for (uint mm = nused - 1u; mm > j; --mm) { idx[mm] = idx[mm - 1u]; val[mm] = val[mm - 1u]; } idx[j] = int(i); val[j] = si; break; } } } float s0 = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { s0 = s0 + probs[idx[j]]; } float s = (s0 < 0.00006103515625f) ? 0.00006103515625f : s0; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { ids[j] = uint(idx[j]); wts[j] = probs[idx[j]] / s * wscale; } } "
)

    (defn dsv4-topk-weights-body ()
        "kernel void form_dsv4_topk_weights (device const float* logits [[buffer(0)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(1)]], device uint* ids [[buffer(2)]], device float* wts [[buffer(3)]], device float* probs [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& ne [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& nused [[buffer(6)]], constant float& wscale [[buffer(7)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (gid != 0u) return; if (ne > 256u) return; if (nused > 8u) return; if (nused > ne) return; float pr[256]; float sc[256]; int idx[8]; for (uint i = 0u; i < ne; ++i) { float z = logits[i]; float sp = (z > 20.0f) ? z : ((z < -20.0f) ? dm_exp(z) : dm_ln(1.0f + dm_exp(z))); float p = dm_sqrt(sp); pr[i] = p; probs[i] = p; sc[i] = p + bias[i]; } for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { idx[j] = -1; } for (uint i = 0u; i < ne; ++i) { for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { if (idx[j] < 0 || sc[i] > sc[idx[j]]) { for (uint mm = nused - 1u; mm > j; --mm) { idx[mm] = idx[mm - 1u]; } idx[j] = int(i); break; } } } float s0 = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { s0 = s0 + pr[idx[j]]; } float s = (s0 < 0.00006103515625f) ? 0.00006103515625f : s0; for (uint j = 0u; j < nused; ++j) { ids[j] = uint(idx[j]); wts[j] = pr[idx[j]] / s * wscale; } } ")

    ; --- the stack's FFN translation unit: Stone 37's unit (the dm_ spine once, the clamped SwiGLU,
    ; scale, axpy, the hash table read and the hash weights) with the biased-top-k kernel appended.
    ; ONE unit, so the two routing regimes cannot drift apart in their softplus or their sqrt.
    (defn dsv4-stack-ffn-source ()
            (str_concat (dsv4-moe-msl-unit)
                    (str_concat (dsv4-hash-select-body)
                     (str_concat (str_concat (dsv4-hash-probs-body) (str_concat (dsv4-hash-wts-body) (dsv4-hash-weights-body)))
        (str_concat (dsv4-topk-weights-body)
        (str_concat (dsv4-topk-split-body)
        (str_concat (dsv4-topk-select-tg-body) (str_concat (dsv4-topk-select-tg6-body) (dom-ffn-appendix)))))))))
    (defn dsv4-stack-ffn-unit ()
        (do
            (print "MSL")
            (print (dsv4-stack-ffn-source))
            (print "END")
            0))

    ; ================= the per-layer decisions, as the body reads them =================
    ; Named here so the recipe is in the body and not only in the carrier. Each takes what the file's own
    ; table gave and returns the decision; none of them takes a default from blk.0.

    ; the per-layer expert count is dim[2] of the gate stack, NEVER deepseek4.expert_count.
    (defn dsv4-layer-expert-count (gate-d2) gate-d2)
    ; the router's width is the logit projection's own out-dim, and it does NOT follow the stack.
    (defn dsv4-router-width (gate-inp-d1) gate-inp-d1)
    ; the routing regime: a layer that CARRIES the table routes by it (ds4.c:10745 tests the pointer).
    (defn dsv4-layer-routes-by-table? (has-tid2eid) has-tid2eid)
    ; RoPE: any nonzero compress ratio means the long-context base and scale (ds4.c:10155/:10162).
    (defn dsv4-layer-rope-compressed? (ratio) (not (eq ratio 0)))

    0)
